[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Quick Start:
  sysrc fjordd_enable=YES
  service fjordd start

  Open http://<host-ip>:3567 in your browser. The first visit asks for the
  setup code fjord wrote on this host (cat /var/db/fjord/setup-code) and
  makes the account; after that every page and the API need a sign-in.
  `fjordd passwd` sets or resets the password; FJORD_AUTH=none in
  fjordd_env turns sign-in off behind a reverse proxy of your own.
  The setup wizard and System dashboard check host readiness and provide
  copyable shell fixes for any missing engine prerequisites.

Host Prerequisites:
  Fjord requires at least one container engine (Podman and/or AppJail).
  See the host prerequisite guide for kernel, package, and PF setup:
    https://fjord.daemonless.io/install/

  - Podman: fjord requires the API socket service running:
      sysrc podman_service_enable=YES
      service podman_service start

  - AppJail: fjord drives appjail-director (sysutils/py-director).
    Requires AppJail 5.5.0 or newer.

  - Firewall (PF): Port publishing on bridge/virtual networks requires
    PF NAT and redirection anchors. If published ports hang or fail,
    check the System dashboard in the web UI.

Stacks are stored in /var/db/fjord/stacks. Additional daemon variables
are documented in %%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/fjordd.
EOM
}
]
